Let the given matrix be
\[ A = \begin{pmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{pmatrix}. \]Then
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x (1 - \cos^2 x) + \cos^2 x (\cos^2 x - 1) \\ &= \cot^2 x \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x (1 - \sin^2 x) \\ &= \cos^2 x \cos^2 x \\ &= \cos^4 x \end{align*}Recall that $\cos^2 x + \sin^2 x = 1,$ so $\cos^2 x = 1 - \sin^2 x = (1 - \sin x)(1 + \sin x).$  Then $\cos^4 x = (\cos^2 x)^2 = (1 - \sin^2 x)^2.$  Since
\begin{align*} \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} \\ &= \frac{-\sin^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \\ &= -1. \end{align*}Then
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \csc^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x)) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x (1 - \cos^2 x) + \cos^2 x (\cos^2 x - 1) \\ &= \cot^2 x \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x (1 - \sin^2 x) = \cos^2 x \cos^2 x = \cos^4 x. \end{align*}
Note that $\sec^2 x = 1 + \tan^2 x,$ $\csc^2 x = 1 + \cot^2 x,$ and $\cot^2 x = \csc^2 x - 1.$  We have
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 0 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x - 1 & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & 0 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} \quad\text{(subtracting 2nd row from 3rd row)} \\ &= \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 0 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & -\sin^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & 0 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} -\sin^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 0 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 0 + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & -\sin^2 x \\ 1 & 0 \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (-\sin^2 x \cot^2 x) + \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= -\sin^2 x \cot^2 x \sec^2 x + \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= -\frac{\sin^2 x \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \sec^2 x + \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= - \cos^2 x \sec^2 x + \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= - \cos^2 x \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} + \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= -1 + \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x (1 - \sin^2 x) - 1 + 1 = \cos^2 x \cos^2 x - 1 + 1 = \cos^4 x. \end{align*}The determinant is $\cos^4 x,$ which ranges from 0 to 1.

\boxed{ \cos^4 x }
\boxed{\cos^4 x}

