The diameter of the circle is the distance between points A(2,5) and B(10,5). The distance formula is $\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2}$. So, the diameter is $\sqrt{(10-2)^2+(5-5)^2} = \sqrt{8^2+0^2} = \sqrt{64} = 8$.
The radius of the circle is half the diameter, so the radius is $r = \frac{8}{2} = 4$.
The area of a circle is given by the formula $A = \pi r^2$. Substituting $r=4$ into the formula, we get $A = \pi (4^2) = 16\pi$.
Therefore, the area of the circle is $16\pi$ square units.

\boxed{16\pi \text{ square units}}
