Let the side length of the cube be $s$. Since the volume of a cube is given by $V = s^3$, we have $s^3 = 0.027$. Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $s = \sqrt[3]{0.027}$. Since $0.3^3 = 0.027$, we have $s = 0.3$ meters.

The surface area of a cube is given by $A = 6s^2$. Substituting $s = 0.3$ meters, we have $A = 6(0.3)^2 = 6(0.09) = 0.54$ square meters.

\boxed{0.54 \text{ square meters}} 
\boxed{0.54}

