The initial volume is $2 \text{ cm} \times 2 \text{ cm} \times 2 \text{ cm} = 8 \text{ cm}^3$. The volume is increased by 19 cubic centimeters to form a larger cube. So the volume of the larger cube is $8 + 19 = 27 \text{ cm}^3$.
Let $x$ be the length of one edge of the new cube. Then $x^3 = 27$, so $x = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3$.
Therefore, the length in centimeters of one edge of the new cube is 3 cm.

\boxed{3 \text{ cm}}
